    "problem_statement": "`unwrap_or` method returns incorrect value for Err instances\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `unwrap_or` method on `Err` instances is not behaving correctly. When called with a default value, it appears to be performing unexpected operations instead of simply returning the default value.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom result import Err\n\n# Create an Err instance\nerr = Err(\"some error\")\n\n# This should return the default value 42\nresult = err.unwrap_or(42)\nprint(f\"Expected: 42, Got: {result}\")\n\n# This should return the default value \"hello\"  \nresult2 = err.unwrap_or(\"hello\")\nprint(f\"Expected: hello, Got: {result2}\")\n\n# This should return None\nresult3 = err.unwrap_or(None)\nprint(f\"Expected: None, Got: {result3}\")\n```\n\nThe method should always return the provided default value when called on an `Err` instance, but it's currently returning unexpected results."
  }
